          "dataType": "value",
          "angle": 180
        }
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": false,
      "data": {
        "title": "Positioning Synthesis",
        "synthesis": "Twilite's best first customers are AI power users, especially developers and technical builders who already feel the limits of chat-only workflows. The broader product can grow toward visual knowledge workers and agent builders, but the launch message should stay sharp: Twilite turns conversations with models into persistent, interactive, visual workspaces.",
        "keyPoints": "• Start with AI-native developers and power users.\n• Sell the escape from chat-only work, not the node graph itself.\n• Expand toward visual thinkers as onboarding gets simpler.\n• Agent builders may become the deepest long-term platform market.\n• Avoid trying to explain Twilite to everyone at once.",
        "openQuestions": "Which demo creates the fastest recognition? Which first-user segment converts most readily? Which onboarding concepts can disappear for non-developers?",
        "notes": "Positioning line: For people who are ready to stop chatting with AI and start working inside what it creates.",
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "twilite-target-audience-qa"
        },
        "_classBinding": {
          "key": "qa-summary",
